<h2 class="prose">And what the axis lines do not do</h2>
<p class="prose"><code>axis</code> chooses what is drawn. The span in the <code>plot</code> call chooses what is computed, and the two are kept apart on purpose: a window that quietly resampled the function would make zooming a chart change the curve.</p>
<div class="step note">axis y auto</div>
<div class="step note">axis x linear</div>

